{

!  Nearest-neighbour fragmentation with capping turned off: the fragment
!  keeps its outermost shell as the real atoms, rather than replacing
!  them with hydrogens.
!
!     group-1-O4Si   silicon and its 4 oxygens, bare
!     group-2-OSi2   oxygen and its 2 silicons, bare
!
!  Davidson (2023) chapter 5 calls these Ln, as against Ln+H.
!
!  This exercises a separate path through MOLECULE.BASE:set_NN_capped_groups.
!  Uncapped, one shell FEWER is requested of do_NN_defragment, because that
!  routine always adds the shell beyond "level" -- the shell which would
!  otherwise be capped. So "level 1, uncapped" asks for level 0 and keeps
!  the extra shell as it stands. The formulae here are what confirm that
!  compensation is right: they must match the heavy atoms of the level 1
!  capped fragments exactly, with the hydrogens dropped.
!
!  Compare tests/short/quartz_NN_fragments_L1:
!
!     capped     H4O4Si     uncapped   O4Si
!     capped     H6OSi2     uncapped   OSi2

   name= quartz

   output_style_options= { real_precision= 4 }

   basis_name= STO-3G

   charge= 0
   multiplicity= 1

   CIF= { file_name= quartz_init.cif }
   process_CIF

   crystal= {
      xray_data= {
         NN_level= 1
         use_NN_capping= FALSE
      }
   }

   put_atom_groups

}
